{"actions":[{"actionCode":null,"actionDate":"2025-02-20","source":"Senate","text":"Read twice and referred to the Committee on Finance.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"10000","actionDate":"2025-02-20","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in Senate","type":"IntroReferral"}],"congress":119,"congressGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/674","cosponsors":[{"bioguideId":"W000805","fullName":"Sen. Warner, Mark R. [D-VA]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-02-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"VA"},{"bioguideId":"S001198","fullName":"Sen. Sullivan, Dan [R-AK]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-02-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"AK"},{"bioguideId":"K000384","fullName":"Sen. Kaine, Tim [D-VA]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-02-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"VA"},{"bioguideId":"T000278","fullName":"Sen. Tuberville, Tommy [R-AL]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-02-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"AL"},{"bioguideId":"K000377","fullName":"Sen. Kelly, Mark [D-AZ]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-02-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"AZ"},{"bioguideId":"C001047","fullName":"Sen. Capito, Shelley Moore [R-WV]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-02-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"WV"},{"bioguideId":"K000383","fullName":"Sen. King, Angus S., Jr. [I-ME]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"I","sponsorshipDate":"2025-02-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"ME"},{"bioguideId":"W000437","fullName":"Sen. Wicker, Roger F. [R-MS]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-02-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MS"},{"bioguideId":"W000790","fullName":"Sen. Warnock, Raphael G. [D-GA]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-02-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"GA"},{"bioguideId":"C001096","fullName":"Sen. Cramer, Kevin [R-ND]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-02-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"ND"},{"bioguideId":"F000463","fullName":"Sen. Fischer, Deb [R-NE]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-02-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NE"},{"bioguideId":"B001230","fullName":"Sen. Baldwin, Tammy [D-WI]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-03-24","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"WI"},{"bioguideId":"M001153","fullName":"Sen. Murkowski, Lisa [R-AK]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-03-24","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"AK"},{"bioguideId":"R000584","fullName":"Sen. Risch, James E. [R-ID]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-03-24","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"ID"},{"bioguideId":"B001267","fullName":"Sen. Bennet, Michael F. [D-CO]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-14","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CO"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-17T05:41:03+00:00","id":"s674-119","introducedDate":"2025-02-20","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-02-20","text":"Read twice and referred to the Committee on Finance."},"laws":[],"number":"674","originChamber":"Senate","policyArea":"Taxation","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"M000934","district":null,"fullName":"Sen. Moran, Jerry [R-KS]","party":"R","state":"KS"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-02-20","actionDesc":"Introduced in Senate","text":"<p><strong>Broadband Grant Tax Treatment Act</strong></p><p>This bill excludes from gross income (for federal tax purposes) certain grants received for broadband deployment.</p><p>As background, contributions of capital to a corporation generally are not taxable income. However, under an exception enacted in 2017 by the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act, grants from a government or civic organization are not contributions to capital and, thus, treated as taxable income. Prior to the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act, the&nbsp;Internal Revenue Service (IRS) considered certain grants from a government or civic organization&nbsp;contributions of capital and, thus, not taxable income.</p><p>The bill specifically excludes from gross income grants received for broadband deployment from the</p><ul><li>National Telecommunications and Information Administration (NTIA) Broadband Equity, Access, and Deployment Program;</li><li>NTIA State Digital Equity Capacity Grant Program;</li><li>NTIA Digital Equity Competitive Grant Program;</li><li>NTIA Enabling Middle Mile Broadband Infrastructure Program;</li><li>Department of Agriculture ReConnect Program;</li><li>Coronavirus State and Local&nbsp;Fiscal Recovery Funds&nbsp;and the Coronavirus Capital Projects Fund; and</li><li>NTIA Tribal Broadband Connectivity Program and the Broadband Infrastructure Program.</li></ul><p>The bill also requires the IRS to issue guidance on the exclusion from gross income of such grants.</p><p>The bill applies to funds received in tax years ending after March 11, 2021.</p>","updateDate":"2026-01-23T18:59:34Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Broadband Grant Tax Treatment Act","type":"s","updateDate":"2026-01-23T19:02:56Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-01-23T19:02:56Z"}
